# DeerStand

Privacy-first multi-tenant hunting club SaaS. Club is the tenant boundary.

## Stack (do not substitute)

- API: ASP.NET Core 9, EF Core, PostgreSQL
- Auth: Zitadel OIDC
- Realtime: SignalR (broadcast-only; mutations via REST)
- Frontend: Next.js 15 App Router, Tailwind (Slate / Emerald / Olive)
- Hosting: Railway (API + Postgres), Vercel (frontend)
- Forbidden: Supabase, Firebase, Prisma, NextAuth

## Layout (mirrors QikLog)

- `src/DeerStand.Core` — domain constants, no IO
- `src/DeerStand.Infrastructure` — EF, migrations, tenant interceptor, RLS SQL
- `src/DeerStand.Api` — minimal APIs + SignalR hub
- Frontend will live under `web/` or `frontend/` when milestone 5 starts
- Map code only under frontend `src/map/`; screens import `ClubMap` only

## Conventions

- File-scoped namespaces, `sealed` by default, nullable on, warnings as errors
- xUnit + Shouldly
- No em dashes in comments, docs, or UI copy
- Conventional Commits, imperative mood
- No secrets in repo; connection strings and Zitadel via environment
- Do not add NuGet/npm packages without asking
- Milestones are gates: do not implement ahead of the current milestone

## Tenant isolation

EF `HasQueryFilter` on ClubId **and** Postgres RLS via `TenantConnectionInterceptor`. Both, always. Cross-tenant misses return 404, not 403.
